ong skin care products  can slow down your skin's natural  exfoliation processes and when this  happens you can end up with clogged  pores breakouts  patches wrinkles and dull skin you can  help your skin along by exfoliating  [Music]  there are two main categories of  exfoliation physical exfoliation and  chemical exfoliation both are great they  each have their pros and cons and you  can use them together as well  [Music]  physical exfoliation is also called  manual or mechanical exfoliation it's  when you buff away dead skin cells a bit  like sanding down wood but hopefully  much much gentler physical exfoliation  is what most people think of when people  talk about exfoliation things like  scrubs and brushes are physical  exfoliants physical exfoliation has a  few advantages firstly the results are  immediate so you can quickly see if  you've exfoliated enough it's also easy  to adjust how gentle or harsh of  physical exfoliant is you just press  harder or buff your skin for longer  there's also a lower chance of an  unexpected reaction because it only  works on the surface of your skin on the  other hand physical exfoliants do only  work on the upper layers of your skin  it's also pretty easy to scrub too hard  and a lot of people purposely scrub too  hard because it feels nice and it feels  like it's working but unfortunately this  causes irritation and over exfoliation  which can make your skin break out and  feel sensitive so the opposite of what  you want to do chemical exfoliation  involves applying a product that helps  skin cells come off more easily without  directly buffing them off some chemical  exfoliants loosen layers of dead skin  cells so that they come off more easily  and in smaller pieces sometimes they'll  act as chemical messengers to change how  quickly skin cells are produced so the  stratum corneum will renew itself more  quickly chemical exfoliation has a lot  of advantages they tend to work more  evenly than physical exfoliants and it's  harder to use them incorrectly a lot of  chemical exfoliants also have additional  benefits on top of exfoliating too like  fading pigment and calming down  inflammation but compared to physical  they tend to be a bit more slow to work  which means you have to be more patient  when you're checking if a new product is  working there's also a higher chance of  irritation and allergic reactions since  they penetrate deeper into your skin  some of them can also make your skin  more sensitive to the sun's harmful UV  rays now that we know what the true  categories of exfoliants are let's look  at the most common ones the most common  physical exfoliants are probably scrubs  scrubs can have a wide range of  different scrubbing particles that vary  from gentle to harsh  some of the gentler particles and scrubs  are plastic microbeads her Hoeber beads  castor sugar and ground oatmeal plastic  microbeads generally don't break down in  the environment and they're too small to  be filtered out from sewage so it's best  to avoid them so you don't contribute to  plastic waste in the environment a lot  of brands are phasing them out as well  so it's very easy to find alternatives  harsher scrubbing particles include  coffee grounds chunky sugar and salt  crystals and crush nut kernels I  personally wouldn't recommend using  these on your face unless you're quite  experienced with exfoliation because  it's really easy to go too hard and end  up with irritated skin an irritation can  cause breakouts and make existing  breakouts even worse  but these harshest scrubs can be really  good for sanding down rough patches on  your body as well as buying scrub  products from the store you can also  make your own scrubs by mixing ground  oatmeal sugar salt or coffee grounds  with oil or water when you're using  scrubs  I recommend buffing lightly in small  circles for a longer time rather than go  really hard for a shorter period it  tends to give you more even and thorough  exfoliation w